c BVE eliminates a variable here, and the refutation then needs the resolvent it wrote.
c The first 37 clauses are 3-clauses over variables 1-9, drawn at random among those that
c 1 2 3 -4 -5 -6 7 8 -9 satisfies until it is their only solution; each variable occurs in 8 to 17.
c The clause -1 -2 4 rules that solution out, and is written as two clauses joined by a fresh
c variable 10: -1 -2 10 and -10 4. Nothing propagates at input and only search refutes the rest.
c Variable 10 occurs in two clauses and every other in at least 8, so BVE tries eliminating 10
c first and accepts it (the resolvent -1 -2 4 has 3 equations, the two clauses 5). With ten
c variables, no more than --bve-residual-dimensions, no clause is held in BVE's core, so this
c holds whatever order BVE reads the clauses in. Eliminating any one of 1-9 would add equations.
p xnf 10 39
